  "narrative": "The new validations and response deadline do not change the supported core landscape. For H18, STK11 loss among KEAP1-intact cells was claimed in the negative, stronger-dependency direction. The independent validation signed estimate is only +0.024 with an upper bound +0.134, which is below the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed direction. This confirms the discovery evidence and supports a reject/close as a threshold-level association in this supplied dataset. For H145, PTEN loss in the very restrictive clean high-quality MSI-negative central-loss-intact context remains point-stable at +0.255, but the independent validation lower bound is +0.094, so the validation interval does not exclude a subthreshold effect. I therefore downgrade this exact context-specific claim to unresolved and close it; this does not challenge PTEN loss itself, whose broader and validated associations remain supported. For H81, the claimed PTEN-loss modification of the KEAP1 association is not supported at threshold: the discovery point is +0.145 and validation is +0.093, with a wide independent interval that includes both opposite-direction and claimed threshold-level modification. I assess it as unresolved but close further pursuit because the PTEN-loss interaction stratum is too small to resolve efficiently. Overall, the accepted descriptive picture in this dataset is that KEAP1 loss and TP53 loss track with higher, less negative dependency_composite values, meaning weaker composite dependency, while SMARCA4 loss, PTEN loss, and MSI-high status track with lower, more negative values, meaning stronger composite dependency. These are dataset-internal associations under the stated contrasts, not causal, knockout-specific, or externally generalizable claims. The next informative step is to move away from tiny co-loss strata and use a less restrictive PTEN central-loss-intact MSI-negative comparison plus the already registered broad technical/biological heterogeneity tests.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 8 synthesis update. The core supplied-dataset landscape remains: KEAP1 loss and TP53 loss associate with weaker composite dependency, i.e. higher/less negative dependency_composite; SMARCA4 loss, PTEN loss, and MSI-high associate with stronger composite dependency, i.e. lower/more negative values. Independent validation continues to support MSI-high and main central-loss claims. New due/new results: H18 is firmly rejected because validation signed upper +0.134 is below threshold; STK11 does not have a threshold-level stronger-dependency association among KEAP1-intact cells. H81 is unresolved/closed; the PTEN-loss interaction with KEAP1 has small signed point estimates and wide independent uncertainty, so no threshold-level effect modification can be claimed. H145 is downgraded from accepted to unresolved/closed because validation, while point-stable, has lower bound below the 0.15 threshold; the broad PTEN association remains accepted separately. Do not overinterpret very small MSI-high or PTEN-loss interaction strata. Proposed next comparison refines H145 by testing PTEN loss among TP53-intact, SMARCA4-intact, KEAP1-intact, MSI-negative cells with a larger and less screen-qualifier-restricted population. Further analysis should prioritize already-registered broad heterogeneity questions: screen batch/library effects, research-signature interactions, mutation-burden and aneuploidy boundary conditions, and this PTEN refinement. If a future validation opportunity is available, prefer interactions with larger strata or borderline but large core-effect contexts over tiny co-loss cells. All current claims are descriptive associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable biological claims."
